            ReleaseNotes = 'See CHANGELOG.md for the full release history. v2.9.0 (proof + honesty release): six new cmdlets (254 -> 260) -- Invoke-TcpkAuthMatrix (vertical authorization matrix), Invoke-TcpkExpiryProbe (server accepts a token past the exp it issued, judged against the server Date header so no local clock is involved), Invoke-TcpkLogoutProbe (does logout revoke anything server-side), Test-TcpkEmbeddedBlobs (formats embedded at arbitrary offsets, structurally validated), Invoke-TcpkJavaDecompile (CFR), Get-TcpkFileStructure (byte patterns). Fixed several views that hid how much they had dropped: the Dashboard top-findings cap, the Hex entropy strip reading only the first 10 MB while its click handler mapped the whole file, Pcap conversation headers that could not scroll, and a hex search that could not find UTF-16LE text. MCP security: tcpk_audit no longer runs the custom actions of an attacker-supplied MSI without an explicit gate, outDir refuses UNC and is confined for write tools, and one boolean parser replaces four. Copilot now connects: the GUI keyed cloud consent off needsKey. v2.8.0 (coverage + honesty release): four new cmdlets -- Test-TcpkJavaSigning (unsigned / mixed-signature JARs), Expand-TcpkPyInstaller (PyInstaller and cx_Freeze carve), Test-TcpkGoRustDeps (Go buildinfo and Rust crate recovery feeding OSV), Test-TcpkQtSurface (QSettings credentials, QProcess, QML, Qt WebEngine). Test-TcpkScanCoverage now reports the conditions that make a clean result meaningless: a packed binary, a single-file bundle above the extractor ceiling, a non-managed target, and a failed CVE lookup. Every artifact TCPK creates moved under the tool folder (work\\out, extract, capture, dump, trace, vulndb, run) so nothing is left in %TEMP% on a target machine. Fixed a dead -Utf8Only code path that silently disabled the Electron detection suite, two bundled-tool paths that resolved outside the tool folder, and a JIT allowlist that suppressed RWX findings on any Vulkan or D3D app. v2.7.1 (scoping + GUI patch): five scanners (WritablePath, AvExclusions, WerExposure, TokenCaches, WerPolicy) now scope findings to the target directory instead of reporting machine-wide state; GUI findings table streams findings live during the audit instead of only after completion. v2.7.0 (19 new cmdlets -- 184 -> 203): the biggest detection release yet. NEW STATIC: gRPC/Protobuf surface (proto files, services, reflection), WebView2 DLL sideloading, AMSI evasion surface, process hollowing / DLL injection / APC injection API sequences, AppDomainManager hijack, .NET AOT detection gate, ClickOnce deployment hijack, MSIX PSF script extraction, phantom DLL planting, diagnostic config exposure, DLL sideload candidates. NEW OS/RUNTIME: COM per-user CLSID hijack, WER crash dump exposure, writable PATH abuse, shared memory DACL audit, window message attack surface, clipboard secret monitoring. NEW EXPLOIT: IL binary patching (Mono.Cecil), IFEO/registry persistence PoC generator. ENHANCED: electron-updater signature bypass + Squirrel detection, WDAC bypass via signed Electron dirs, NuGet vuln scanning, severity re-baseline (10 rules), exploit-map linkage fixes. HEX WORKBENCH: PE structure overlay, entropy heatmap, XOR/decode toolkit, binary diff. AGENTIC: hash-based tab routing (#tab=N), full 13-tab documentation with screenshots. 5 new test files. v2.6.1 (Asar supply-chain audit + UI fix): the Asar tab gains an npm audit action -- OSV / GHSA CVE matching plus npm-registry deprecation flags. v2.6.0 (detection uplift + accuracy + UI pass): severity-anchored CVSS v4.0, Electron-aware provenance gate, crypto-constant / TypeNameHandling / cross-assembly taint IL verdicts, token-privilege / integrity-level checks, CVE native-banner scan, Dashboard + DLL Decompiler GUI tabs, MCP decompiler. v2.5.0 (GUI + workbench pass): Hex Data Inspector, Process Monitor tab, Runtime / Asar / Hex in workbench. v2.4.4 (stable): interception, secret recovery, credential liveness, Frida bypass, Credential Manager extraction.'
